response:
 To express $$
\sqrt{6\frac{1}{4}}
$$ as a common fraction in simplest form, we first convert the mixed number $$
6\frac{1}{4}
$$ to an improper fraction. The mixed number $$
6\frac{1}{4}
$$ is equivalent to the improper fraction $$
\frac{25}{4}
$$. Then, we take the square root of $$
\frac{25}{4}
$$, which is $$
\sqrt{\frac{25}{4}}
$$, and simplify it to $$
\frac{5}{2}
$$. </think> <answer> 5/2 </answer>

